    "folder": "0507 核聚变能源能否很快加入美国电网？",
    "titleZh": "核聚变能源能否很快加入美国电网？",
    "title": "Could fusion energy soon join the U.S. power grid?",
    "topicEn": "Technology",
    "topicZh": "科技",
    "byline": "By Adam Kovac, Scientific American, Published April 28, 2026",
    "paragraphs": [
      "The fusion energy start-up Commonwealth Fusion Systems aims to bring its first power plant online by the early 2030s, but daunting technical hurdles remain",
      "On Tuesday a fusion energy start-up announced that it has applied to join a U.S. power grid—a first that could one day see households and businesses powered by nuclear fusion.",
      "Commonwealth Fusion Systems is looking to join a power grid that is operated by PJM Interconnection and provides 182,000 megawatts of power to more than 67 million people living in 13 states and Washington, D.C. But technical hurdles to bringing fusion online remain— one major obstacle is actually producing a stable fusion reaction that generates more energy than it consumes.",
      "The application process requires a potential energy provider to provide extensive technical information to the grid operator, including descriptions of the planned fuel type. In Commonwealth's case, the company is developing a tokamak reactor design that uses powerful magnetic fields to create and insulate a highly energetic cloud of particles called a plasma until it's hot enough for those particles to fuse. It's a process that mimics the nuclear reactions in the sun, including the particles involved: isotopes of hydrogen called deuterium and tritium. The promise of the device is that a fusion reaction could feasibly generate limitless clean energy. That energy, in the form of heat, is used to boil water into steam, which then pushes a turbine to produce electricity.",
      "Much of that process remains theoretical, however, because physicists have yet to prove that fusion can work as a large-scale power source. Recent results from Germany's Wendelstein 7-X demonstrated it could contain superheated plasma for 43 seconds. And its rival, the Joint European Torus, was apparently able to accomplish that feat for a full minute before its reactor was retired in 2023. While such capabilities are impressive, there is still a long way to go before a fusion device could be connected to a grid. Commonwealth plans to open its first power plant, called ARC (for \"affordable, robust, compact\"), in Virginia in the early 2030s. And the company aims to demonstrate an initial model, called SPARC (for \"smallest possible ARC\"), in 2027.",
      "Commonwealth has demonstrated some success: The company's toroidal field magnet technology was validated by the Department of Energy in September 2025. The superconducting magnets generate the magnetic field that is used to contain the high-temperature plasma generated by a fusion reaction. But Commonwealth has yet to test the full system.",
      "Commonwealth co-founder and CEO Bob Mumgaard said in a statement that the company is committed \"to delivering the benefits of fusion, and enabling a future with abundant, secure energy, [which] means that we're not just proving fusion physics works—we're showing exactly how fusion power plant watts get from our machine to the customer, working with the grid and a utility.\"",
      "\"By becoming the first fusion energy developer to enter a major grid operator's interconnection queue, we're demonstrating that when you're serious about building a power plant in the early 2030s, you act now,\" he said. \"This is execution.\"",
      "Commonwealth's application will likely take years to be approved; the company will navigate a complex process that will include several impact studies and other analyses, as well as reviews of the its capabilities, readiness, safety controls and other compliance.",
      "PJM said in a statement that it's \"excited about the diversity of resources that have applied to connect to the grid through the first cycle of PJM's reformed interconnection process.\"",
      "\"Bringing new generation online is critical to maintaining grid reliability as demand continues to increase, and our process is designed to improve the certainty, speed and discipline of project review.\""
    ],
    "paragraphTranslations": [
      "核聚变能源初创公司 Commonwealth Fusion Systems 计划在 2030 年代初投运其首座发电厂，但艰巨的技术挑战依然存在",
      "本周二，一家聚变能源初创公司宣布，已向美国电网提交接入申请—— 这是此类申请的首例，未来有一天或许能让家庭和企业用上核聚变电力。",
      "Commonwealth Fusion Systems 正寻求接入由 PJM 互联运营的电网。该电网覆盖 13 个州和华盛顿特区，为逾 6700 万人提供电力服务，供电能力达 182,000 兆瓦。然而，要让聚变电力真正投入电网，技术挑战依然严峻—— 其中一个主要障碍，是如何真正产生稳定且实现能量净增益的聚变反应。",
      "根据申请流程，潜在的发电商需要向电网运营商提供详尽的技术信息，包括对拟使用燃料类型的说明。以 Commonwealth 为例，该公司正在开发一种托卡马克反应堆设计，利用强磁场形成并约束一团高能粒子云，即所谓等离子体，直至其温度高到足以让粒子发生聚变。这一过程模拟了太阳内部的核反应，包括其中涉及的粒子：氢的同位素氘和氚。该装置的前景在于，聚变反应理论上有望产生近乎无限的清洁能源。这些能量以热的形式释放，用来将水煮沸成蒸汽，进而推动涡轮机发电。",
      "然而，这一过程在很大程度上仍停留在理论层面，因为物理学家尚未证明聚变能够成为大规模电力来源。德国 Wendelstein 7-X 装置的最新结果显示，它能将超高温等离子体约束 43 秒。而其竞争对手 Joint European Torus 在 2023 年退役前，据称也曾实现同样壮举，将等离子体约束了整整一分钟。这样的能力固然令人瞩目，但要让聚变装置真正接入电网，仍有很长的路要走。 Commonwealth 计划于 2030 年代初在弗吉尼亚州投运其首座聚变电站 ARC，名称取 affordable、robust、compact 之意，即“经济、可靠、紧凑”。公司还计划在 2027 年展示其原型装置 SPARC，即“最小可行 ARC”。",
      "Commonwealth 已取得一定进展：2025 年 9 月，该公司的环向场磁体技术获得美国能源部验证。这些超导磁体能够产生磁场，用以约束聚变反应生成的高温等离子体。不过，Commonwealth 尚未对整套系统展开测试。",
      "Commonwealth 联合创始人兼首席执行官 Bob Mumgaard 在一份声明中表示，公司致力于“让聚变能带来切实益处，迈向一个能源充裕且安全的未来。这意味着我们不只是在证明聚变物理原理可行—— 我们还在具体展示，聚变电站产生的电力如何通过与电网和电力公司的协作，从我们的设备输送到客户手中。”",
      "“作为首家进入主要电网运营商并网申请队列的聚变能源开发商，我们正在证明：如果你真的打算在 2030 年代初建成一座电站，就必须现在行动，”他说，“这就是执行力。”",
      "Commonwealth 的申请可能需要数年才能获批；公司将经历一套复杂流程，包括多项影响评估和其他分析，以及对其技术能力、准备状态、安全控制措施和其他合规事项的审查。",
      "PJM 在一份声明中表示，他们对“在 PJM 改革后的并网流程首个周期内，申请接入电网的资源类型更加多元感到振奋”。",
      "“随着电力需求持续增长，新增电源的并网对维持电网可靠性至关重要，而我们这套流程正是为了提升项目审核的确定性、速度和严谨性。”"
    ],
