    "answerChoice": "D",
    "answerTranslation": "The instinct to ban books in schools seems to come from a desire to protect children from things that the adults doing the banning find upsetting or offensive. These adults often seem unable to see beyond harsh language or gruesome imagery to the books' educational and artistic value, or to recognize that language and imagery may be integral to showing the harsh, gruesome truths of the books' subjects.",
