    "byline": "By Marc Champion, Bloomberg, Published July 7, 2026",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Tehran's Grand Mosalla Mosque, where the late Ayatollah Ali Khamenei was held in state this weekend, is an extraordinary building. In a country filled with exquisitely tiled, millennium-old houses of worship, this one is a plain, brutalist product of the 1979 revolution whose sole virtue is its size. With a main prayer hall that spans multiple World Cup soccer fields, it is a still unfinished monument to the sheer scale of religious fervor that Iran's supreme leader sought to institutionalize.",
      "When I went to Friday prayers in the mosque a decade ago, it was clear Khamenei had failed. Attendance was sparse. When the cleric leading the service began punching the air to chant \"Death to America! Death to Israel! Death to the Infidel!\" the response was mechanical and insincere. As an American infidel, I didn't take part. My neighbor asked where I was from and brightened visibly when I told him. \"Ah, I like America,\" he said, citing its freedoms.",
      "This week's ceremonies are unfolding in the same place but a different world. There are far too many mourners for the indoor prayer hall and the sense is of defiance and fury. The \"Death to America!\" chants are vengeful and heartfelt. When I visited, the 2015 nuclear deal was still in effect and many Iranians had hoped the days of their nation's zero-sum confrontation with Washington were over. Now the countries have been at war and the regime is trying to revive the legitimizing myth that lost its power in Khamenei's later years and left him ruling by violence alone. The war has made a cruel, despised and out-of-touch old man into a martyr.",
      "Khamenei's six-day funeral is high political theater. The state invited world leaders and Iranians from around the country to come to Mosalla and show their love and respect. The procession is supposed to move to other religious centers including Karbala, in Iraq, where just a week ago Shiites converged from all around the world to celebrate their faith's origin story in the martyrdom of the Prophet Mohammad's grandson, Hussein ibn Ali. The timing, more than four months after Khamenei's killing, is choreographed. The connection is intended to be made.",
      "Pro-Iran militias in Iraq called on their members to turn out in force. Harakat al-Nujaba leader Akram al-Kaabi told them in a Telegram post their presence would be \"no less significant than fighting these vile Zionists on the battlefields of Jihad.\"",
      "In all, Iranian officials say they expect 20 million people to pay their respects to Khamenei, which would make this the largest funeral in recorded history. Nobody will be able to count the true number who attend this rolling ceremony, but it's likely to reach into the millions, and why not? Josef Stalin also built a state on cruelty and repression, killing vastly more of his own people than has Khamenei. Millions turned out to mourn his loss, too, and he wasn't killed by a foreign power, alongside his 14-month-old granddaughter. Stalin died of a stroke after a drinking binge."
    ],
    "paragraphTranslations": [
      "本周末，已故伊朗最高领袖阿亚图拉·阿里·哈梅内伊的遗体停放在德黑兰莫萨拉大清真寺这座非凡的建筑中。在伊朗这个遍布精美瓷砖装饰、不乏千年历史宗教场所的国家中，这座清真寺却是 1979 年革命时期一座朴素的、粗野主义的建筑，唯一的优点就是规模巨大。它的主礼拜大厅足以横跨数个世界杯足球场，至今仍未完工，却像一座纪念碑，纪念着伊朗最高领袖曾试图制度化的宗教狂热究竟有多么庞大。",
      "10 年前，我曾去这座清真寺参加周五礼拜，很明显，当时哈梅内伊是失败的。参加礼拜的人寥寥无几。当主持礼拜的神职人员开始挥拳高呼“美国去死！以色列去死！异教徒去死！”时，人们的反应机械而虚伪。作为一个美国异教徒，我没有跟着喊。旁边的人在我告诉他我来自美国时明显高兴起来。“啊，我喜欢美国，”他说，并提到了美国的自由。",
      "本周的悼念仪式在同一地点举行，但世界已经不同。室内礼拜大厅远远容纳不下前来哀悼的人群，现场弥漫着一种反抗与愤怒的气息。“美国去死！”的口号充满复仇的怒火，发自肺腑。我当年到访伊朗时，2015 年的核协议仍然有效，许多伊朗人曾以为，自己的国家与美国长期零和对抗的日子终于要过去了。如今，两国已陷入战争，伊朗政权正试图重现其合法性神话。然而，这套神话在哈梅内伊晚年已然失效，只剩下他依靠暴力维系统治。战争把一个残暴、遭人憎恨、与现实脱节的老人，塑造成了烈士。",
      "哈梅内伊为期 6 天的葬礼，是一场高度政治化的表演。伊朗政府邀请世界各国领导人和来自全国各地的伊朗人前往莫萨拉，表达他们的爱戴与敬意。送葬队伍还计划前往其他宗教中心，包括伊拉克的卡尔巴拉。就在 1 周前，来自世界各地的什叶派穆斯林刚刚聚集在那里，纪念先知穆罕默德的外孙侯赛因·伊本·阿里殉难这一信仰起源故事。哈梅内伊遇刺 4 个多月后才举行这场葬礼，这一时间安排显然经过精心设计，目的就是要让人们建立这种联系。",
      "伊拉克境内亲伊朗民兵组织号召成员大规模出席。努贾巴运动领导人阿克拉姆·卡比在 Telegram 上发帖告诉他们，他们的到场“其意义绝不亚于在圣战战场上同这些卑劣的犹太复国主义者作战”。",
      "伊朗官员表示，他们预计总共会有 2,000 万人前来悼念哈梅内伊。如果属实，这将成为有记录以来规模最大的葬礼。没有人能够统计参加这场盛大葬礼的确切人数，但很可能达到数百万，这也不难理解。约瑟夫·斯大林同样建立了一个依靠残酷和镇压运转的国家，他杀害的本国民众远远多于哈梅内伊，也有数百万人前往哀悼他的离世。而且，斯大林并不是被外国势力所害，也不是和自己 14 个月大的外孙女一同遇害，而是在一次酗酒后中风去世的。"
    ],
