    "folder": "0710 葬礼过后才是危机开始：我们该如何看待这场伊朗国葬？2",
    "titleZh": "葬礼过后才是危机开始：我们该如何看待这场伊朗国葬？2",
    "title": "Ali Khamenei Was a Monster. The US Made Him a Martyr · Part 2",
    "topicEn": "Politics",
    "topicZh": "政治",
    "byline": "By Marc Champion, Bloomberg, Published July 7, 2026",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Iran's leaders, including Khamenei, were out of ideas back in January. The vast majority of the population loathed them. The revolution and subsequent eight-year war with Iraq that shaped their world view meant nothing to this year's protesters, most of whom hadn't been born in 1979. The Islamic Republic needed a new legitimizing myth. It hopes it has found one now in the story of Khamenei's martyrdom and the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps' defense of Iran against the combined military might of the US and Israel.",
      "For IRGC commander Ahmad Vahidi and other regime leaders, this funeral is probably more important than their 60-day negotiations with the US. It is impossible to know whether this attempt to rejuvenate the Islamic Republic will succeed. Even if 20 million people do show up to look at Khamenei's coffin, in a nation of more than 90 million that would merely confirm what we already knew - that the regime still has a bedrock of faithful supporters, even as it lost the majority.",
      "And yes, a handful of international leaders did show up for the funeral, as did a few lower-ranking officials from the likes of China, Russia, India and - most significantly - Saudi Arabia. But this showed less Iran's strength than its continued international isolation.",
      "The economy will remain in terrible shape when this funeral is over. Year-on-year inflation will still be closing on 90%. The replacements for Khamenei and other leaders killed in the opening hours of the ridiculously named \"Operation Epic Fury\" will face the same difficult decisions as before. How far can the Islamic Republic afford to relax rules on female dress, rock concerts, dissidence and other hallmarks of the decadent West it's fighting, before it stops being the Islamic Republic? How does the complex coalition of regime factions that now rules the country restore the economy without reconciling with the US or loosening the IRGC's corrupt grip on much of it? How does the regime secure the nation's water supplies, after failing to husband them for decades?",
      "These questions and more will return once the war's rally-aroundthe-flag effects fade. Which is why Vahidi, arguably now the most powerful man in Iran, may not be in a hurry to see the conflict end, unless that happens on terms that look like a clear victory and leave the Islamic Republic with more money and options than it had before the war.",
      "Many will say this argues for a return to war to \"finish the job.\" But if Operation Epic Fury and Khamenei's funereal drama prove anything, it is that air strikes can’t achieve the regime change that such finality would require. They just undermine the story that the West has to offer like-minded Iranians, and make the job harder for those who would actually have to finish it. For if and when that happens, American and Israeli fighter pilots won't be the ones responsible. That will fall to Iranians, drawn from the 70 million-plus people who didn't take part in the IRGC's funeral theater."
    ],
    "paragraphTranslations": [
      "早在今年 1 月，包括哈梅内伊在内的伊朗领导层就已经束手无策。大多数民众对他们深恶痛绝。塑造他们世界观的革命以及随后长达 8 年的两伊战争，对于如今的抗议者来说毫无意义，因为他们大多数人甚至在 1979 年都还没有出生。伊朗伊斯兰共和国需要一个新的合法性神话。现在，它希望能在哈梅内伊殉难，以及伊斯兰革命卫队抵御美以联军、保卫伊朗的叙事中找到这个神话。",
      "对伊斯兰革命卫队司令艾哈迈德·瓦希迪以及其他政权领导人来说，这场葬礼的重要性，很可能超过他们与美国进行的 60 天谈判。我们无法预知这次重振伊斯兰共和国的尝试能否成功。即便真的有 2,000 万人前来瞻仰哈梅内伊的灵柩，在一个人口超过 9,000 万的国家里，这也不过是证明了我们早已知道的事实：即便政权已经失去多数民众支持，它仍然拥有一批忠实的信徒。",
      "是的，确实有少数国际领 dao 人出席了葬礼，也有一些来自 ZG、俄罗斯、印度以及— 最重要的是— 沙特阿拉伯等国的较低级别官员到场。但这与其说显示了伊朗的实力，不如说显示出伊朗仍然处于国际孤立之中。",
      "这场葬礼结束后，伊朗经济仍将处于糟糕状态。同比通胀率仍将逼近 90%。在名字荒谬的“史诗怒火行动”开始阶段就被杀害的哈梅内伊和其他领 dao 人的继任者们，仍将面对和过去一样艰难的抉择。伊朗伊斯兰共和国究竟能在女性着装、摇滚音乐会、异见人士以及其他它所反对的“颓废西方”标志的限制上放宽到什么程度，才能不至于丧失其伊斯兰共和国的本质？如今统治这个国家的复杂政权派系联盟，如果不与美国和解，或者不削弱伊斯兰革命卫队对大部分经济领域的腐败控制，又该如何恢复经济？在数十年未能妥善管理水资源之后，这个政权又该如何保障国家供水？",
      "一旦战争带来的“聚旗效应”消退，这些问题以及更多问题都会重新浮现。这也是为什么，瓦希迪，目前来看伊朗最有权势的人，或许并不急于结束这场冲突。除非冲突以一场看似彻底的胜利告终，并让伊斯兰共和国获得比战前更多的资金和选择。",
      "许多人会说，这证明美国应该重返战争，以“完成任务”。但如果“史诗怒火行动”和哈梅内伊的葬礼大戏证明了什么，那就是光凭空袭无法实现终局性要求所需要的政权更迭，而只会削弱西方向志同道合的伊朗人兜售的故事，并让那些真正必须完成这项任务的人面临更大困难。因为如果有一天伊朗政权真的发生更迭，负责完成它的不会是美国和以色列的战斗机飞行员，而是伊朗民众， 7,000 多万没有参与伊斯兰革命卫队葬礼演出的民众。"
    ],
