    "folder": "0825为什么总有人骑着巨响无比的摩托车炸街？",
    "titleZh": "为什么总有人骑着巨响无比的摩托车炸街？",
    "title": "Why Do Some Motorcycles Make So Much Noise?",
    "topicEn": "Technology",
    "topicZh": "科技",
    "byline": "By Michelle Delio, Salon.com, Published May 19, 2003 听课笔记",
    "paragraphs": [
      "The classic Harley sound is pure machine music—valves clattering, push rods jamming up and down, gears whining—all rattling up through that thumping exhaust noise in an ascending roar. But the sound is a big problem for Harley-Davidson engineers, who have to carefully incorporate new technology into their factory-fresh models to suit modern environmental, noise, pollution and performance standards without destroying the sound, which the company considers to be a trademark and one of the fundamental reasons many people opt to purchase a Harley.",
      "\"I was 5 years old the first time I heard a Harley. I thought the heavens had opened up and that Thor was smashing the world to atoms,\" Dave Nichols, editor of Easyriders magazine, recalled. \"You could hear that Harley thunder coming from miles away. It was, and is, the sound of rebellion. It is a sound as unique as American rock 'n' roll.\" \"Is the Harley sound as big an attraction to sales as Harley-Davidson thinks? Abso-fuckin'-lutely!\"",
      "\"Harleys have become civilized over the past few years and that's a shame. The last thing most people want is a mannerly motorcycle,\" said Elliot Borin, former editor in chief of Supercycle magazine. \"Harleys don't even sound right anymore.\"",
      "Letters from readers:",
      "1. Harley-Davidson has spent this last 100 years building a brand. By this point in their history, a brand is all they have left. The soul of their motorcycles left when they ceased being a voice of youthful rebellion, and started being a voice of upper-middle-class pseudo-rebellion. The Harley riders making their pilgrimage to Milwaukee this summer are lawyers and stockbrokers trying to take back a piece of their 1960s and '70s memories, armed with overpriced bikes and matching Harley-Davidson branded jackets, boots, gloves and underwear. They don't live to ride, they live for others to think they live to ride.",
      "2. The \"Harley sound\" is nothing more than an overhyped accessory, the equivalent of a Gucci handbag for the midlife crisis brigade or a signed Sonny Barger photo for the soap-averse crew. They wouldn't be waxing quite so lyrical about the beauty of noise if I came and parked outside their houses and blared Bee Gees music all day.",
      "3. \"Loud pipes save lives?\" Not when I'm removing my sword from the next Harley rider who interrupts my sleep, my phone conversations, recording sessions or general right to a little peace and quiet. Or perhaps I'll blast Barry Manilow outside my local riders' domiciles at 2:30 in the morning. Don't like it? Don't be such a prude, man.",
      "4. The loud Harley noise destroys hearing bit by bit, permanently. Eight hours a day at 85 decibels will cause damage—and long rides sitting on a box that can easily crank out 100 decibels will graduate a rider nicely into the category of moderately deaf. That's the reason the guy's \"ol' lady\" couldn't hear him coming on his V-Rod—she's lost too much of her hearing.",
      "5. It may be hard for you to understand, but the sound of your pipes is about as charming and about as welcome as the sound of loud sex coming through a thin wall at a motel. Put a muzzle on it, folks."
    ],
    "paragraphTranslations": [
      "经典的哈雷声浪简直就是纯粹的机械音乐—— 气门咔嗒作响，推杆猛烈地上下运动，齿轮发出尖细的呜鸣；所有这些机械声响都随着低沉有力的排气声一路震荡上涌，最终汇成不断攀升的轰鸣。然而，这种声音却给哈雷戴维森的工程师出了一个大难题：他们必须小心翼翼地把新技术融入刚刚出厂的新车型，使其符合现代的环保、噪声、污染排放和性能标准，同时又不能毁掉这种声音—— 公司把它视为自己的标志性特征，并认为它正是许多人选择购买哈雷的根本原因之一。",
      "Easyriders 杂志编辑戴夫·尼科尔斯回忆道：“我五岁那年第一次听见哈雷。我觉得仿佛天门洞开，雷神托尔正在把整个世界砸成碎片。几英里之外，你就能听见哈雷那雷鸣般的声响。那曾经是—— 如今仍然是—— 反叛之声。它和美国摇滚乐一样独一无二。”\n\n“哈雷的声音真像哈雷戴维森自己认为的那样，对销量有那么大的吸引力吗？当然—— 百分之百—— 是！”",
      "“这几年，哈雷变得越来越‘文明’了，而这真让人遗憾。大多数人最不想要的，就是一辆彬彬有礼的摩托车，”Supercycle 杂志前主编埃利奥特·博林说，“如今的哈雷听起来一点都不对了。”",
      "读者来信：",
      "1. 哈雷戴维森花了整整一百年来打造一个品牌。发展到今天，这个品牌也已经是它唯一剩下的东西了。当哈雷不再是年轻人的反叛声音，而开始代表中上阶层的“伪反叛”时，它的摩托车也就失去了灵魂。这个夏天，那些像朝圣一样赶往密尔沃基的哈雷骑手，不过是一群律师和股票经纪人试图找回自己在 20 世纪六七十年代的一点青春记忆，他们骑着价格虚高的摩托，穿着全套相互配套的哈雷品牌夹克、靴子、手套，甚至内裤。他们不是为了骑行而活；他们活着，是为了让别人以为他们为了骑行而活。",
      "2. 所谓“哈雷之声”，不过是一件被过度吹捧的配饰罢了—— 对那支“中年危机大军”来说，它就相当于一只古驰手袋；对那帮仿佛对香皂敬而远之的硬核骑手来说，它又相当于一张桑尼·巴格的亲笔签名照片。要是我把车停在他们家门口，一整天开足音量播放比吉斯，我敢说他们就不会再如此诗意盎然地赞美“噪音之美”了。",
      "3.“很响的排气管能救命？”等我把剑从下一个打扰我睡觉、电话交谈、录音工作，或者侵犯我享有一点安宁清静之基本权利的哈雷骑手身上拔出来时，可就救不了他的命了。又或者，我可以凌晨两点半跑到附近那些骑手的住所外面，把巴里·曼尼洛的歌开到震天响。你不喜欢？哥们儿，别这么假正经嘛。",
      "4. 哈雷巨大的噪声会一点一点地损害人的听力，而且这种损伤是永久性的。每天在 85 分贝的噪声环境中持续暴露 8 小时会造成损伤；而如果长途骑行时坐在箱子上，箱子可以轻易制造出接近 100 分贝的声音，会让骑手最后很妙地进入中等失聪的范畴。这就是为什么那个骑手的老伴听不到他骑着大排量摩托来了，因为她已经丢失了太多她的听力。",
      "5. 你也许很难理解，但你那排气管发出的声音有多迷人、多受欢迎呢，大概就跟在汽车旅馆里隔着一堵薄墙听见隔壁大声做爱的动静差不多。各位，给它戴上个嘴套吧。"
    ],
